 "notes": "Dark photon kinetic mixing limit from recasting ORGAN Phase 1a axion haloscope data (63.2-67.1 ueV) via chi = g_agamma*B/(m_gamma'*|cos theta|), Eq. (7), B0=11.5 T. Curve traced from vector paths of Fig. 1 (figures/DarkPhoton_Haloscopes_ORGAN_Closeup.pdf in the e-print): opaque crimson region = fixed-polarisation scenario with |cos theta| ~= sqrt(0.03), which the paper presents as its main (conservative) result and uses throughout Fig. 2; the transparent random-polarisation curve was not used. Axis calibration from tick labels (linear 60-80 ueV in mass, log 1e-14 to 1e-8 in chi); extracted the lower boundary of the excluded region and binned to 200 points (log-space mean per bin) to preserve the spiky per-scan-step structure. Paper assumes rho_DM = 0.45 GeV/cm^3, matching the compilation convention, so no rescaling applied. 95% CL. Paper also derives scalar/dilaton g_phigamma and QEMD g_aAB limits (Fig. 3), but the dark photon limit is presented as the headline result ('the most sensitive to date in some regions').",
